== check main.hero
check exit 0
build  exit 1
error[ffi_callback_type]: `visit` of `nftw` is not the callback the header declares — clang read the header, and it says `int (*)(const char *, const struct stat *, int, struct FTW *)`
  at main.hero:11:5
     |
  11 |     function nftw(path: cstr lent, visit: (function(path: cstr, sb: Stat lent, flag: i32, @at: Ftw) -> i32), fds: i32,…
     |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  note: spec § 13: a callback is declared with the header's own parameter and result types — each parameter at its width and sign, and `()` where the header says void
  note: a pointee the header marks `const` has no spelling here unless it is `const char *`, which is `cstr` — design.md Part 8 wart 19 names this and the four causes measured beside it
